refore:\n- B1 is true exactly when W1 is true.\n\nW1 says “THIS BOX IS EMPTY,” so:\n- W1 is true iff the gem is NOT in WHITE.\n- Therefore B1 = W1 = “gem is not in WHITE.”\n\nK1 says: “Either boxes next to WHITE contain gems or the other two boxes are empty.”  \nThe boxes next to WHITE are BLUE and BLACK, which are also “the other two boxes” besides WHITE. With exactly one gem, either the gem is in BLUE/BLACK, or it is in WHITE and both BLUE and BLACK are empty. So K1 is always true.\n\nSince K1 is true, we still need at least one all-false box. B1 and W1 are false only when the gem is in WHITE. If the gem were not in WHITE, B1 and W1 would both be true, leaving no all-false box. Thus the gem must be in WHITE.\n\nFINAL: gem=WHITE; B1=F; W1=F; K1=T"}
