t in BLACK.\n- W1 is true iff the gem is in WHITE.\n- K1 says the boxes next to BLACK contain the gems, i.e. the gem is in BLUE or WHITE.\n\nCase gem in BLACK:  \nB1 = F, W1 = F, K1 = F → no all-true box, invalid.\n\nCase gem in WHITE:  \nB1 = T, W1 = T, K1 = T → no all-false box, invalid.\n\nCase gem in BLUE:  \nB1 = T, W1 = F, K1 = T → BLUE is all-true, WHITE is all-false, BLACK is all-true. This satisfies all rules.\n\nFINAL: gem=BLUE; B1=T; W1=F; K1=T"}
