nt true and K1 false, B1 must be true; then W1 true. Thus white has gems, K1 false. Check conditions satisfied.\n\nLet's formulate.", "content": "- K1: “The black box is blue” is false, because the black box is black, not blue.\n- Since at least one box must be all-true, at least one statement must be true. K1 is false, so either B1 or W1 must be true.\n- B1 says “a box next to the black box contains the gems.” The only box next to the black box is the WHITE box, so B1 is true if and only if WHITE contains the gems.\n- W1 says “the statement above this one is true,” referring to B1. So W1 has the same truth value as B1.\n- Therefore, for at least one statement to be true, B1 must be true. This means WHITE contains the gems, and W1 is also true.\n- K1 remains false, satisfying the requirement that at least one box is all-false.\n\nFINAL: gem=WHITE; B1=T; W1=T; K1=F"}
