ACK. \"The right box's statement is true\" -> all three? K1 true in all so Black true always. No unique.\n\nGiven no unique, I will final with underdetermination.", "content": "Under the literal displayed-statement rules, the puzzle is not uniquely solvable.  \nK1 must be true, because no box has two displayed statements, so no box has two false statements.  \nThat leaves three valid gem placements: BLUE, WHITE, or BLACK.\n\nFINAL: NO_UNIQUE_SOLUTION; K1=T; B1/W1 vary with gem location"}
