s false, and all statements would be false — invalid.\n- If gems are in WHITE: W1 is true, the WHITE box is true, so K1 is true. This gives at least one all-true box and at least one all-false box.\n\nFINAL: gem=WHITE; B1=F; W1=T; K1=T"}
